        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0174" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851T.001/16: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of President Roosevelt in
                        French West Africa</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Glassford</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dakar</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-23T13:00:00+00:00">June 23, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 24—2:56 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>381. Following telegram has been sent to Algiers.</p>
                <p>182, June 23, 1 p.m. For Murphy. Can you give me any further information on the
                    attitude of the Liberation Committee as it has developed toward Boisson.</p>
                <p>The Gaullists and other critics of the Governor General ([Amis de Combat?],
                    Action Républicaine, Union National [des Anciens?] Combattants) are disposed to
                    say that Boisson has sold Dakar to the Americans who are therefore keeping him
                    in office; that in fact the Governor General is now relying to a great extent on
                    American support and is still in office because [of] us. For the time being at
                    any rate this reaction appears to be prompted entirely by exasperation <pb
                        facs="0175" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/> with Boisson’s tenacity and not by any
                    real mistrust of our intentions with respect to French West Africa.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Glassford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
